hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1031","Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abi Adiy narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, H. Yahya bin narrated to us Hakim, Yazid bin Harun told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Ibn Buhayna, he said: “He led us in prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and he mentioned the hadith. Yahya bin Hakim said in his hadith: So we glorified him, but when he turned back, he went away and did not come back. Al-Fadl said: So they glorified him, but he went away and did not come back."
"1032","Ahmad bin Mani’ and Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas.” He got up in the two rak'ahs, so they glorified Him, and he completed them, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness when he left, then he said: Did you see me sitting? I did what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing.” This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Mani’. Abu Bakr said: I do not think that Abu Muawiyah is mistaken in the wording of this chain of transmission."
